en them","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-78b6-be4b-6fba33137af0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which networking protocol is used to transfer files between two computers?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"FTP was built for uploading and downloading files, and its classic design uses separate control and data connections.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7b7c-a59a-c1550b220b8a","description":"FTP","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7f63-bf75-44652e8789b5","description":"SSH","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-707f-9106-a8e466ffdbc3","description":"HTTP","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-754d-a9d9-25e543cb1786","description":"SMTP","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7780-8f08-7f5fe07b8561","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the more common name for the plant Viscum Album?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Mistletoe is an evergreen parasitic plant that grows on trees and gets some of its water and nutrients from its host.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7ab4-a040-23addc96c204","description":"Mistletoe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7fed-bb5d-50baae8152cc","description":"Tomato","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-745a-a436-7a72002293fe","description":"Sunflower","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7fc1-8a0c-a7ac45605ef0","description":"Marijuana","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7736-a710-77c24f7ce013","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who is credited with discovering penicillin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Alexander Fleming\u2019s observation helped launch the antibiotic era, though other scientists later developed penicillin into a practical treatment.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-772e-af46-be00f172ab59","description":"Alexander Fleming","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-78d6-b232-1783808036a2","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":false}