italis obtained?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Foxglove contains cardiac glycosides such as digoxin, which can strengthen heart contractions but are toxic at excessive doses.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7793-9cdd-9160451a5019","description":"Foxglove","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7b49-9eb0-03ffc25c81db","description":"Nightshade","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-791e-82fa-d879a2cdb38d","description":"Bamboo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7844-936e-0efbf697c511","description":"Coconut","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-728d-a187-7b626468ac8b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of oxen?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A yoke can mean a pair of oxen working together, as well as the wooden device used to harness them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-75b9-ba3d-97b847a7008d","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-79a6-853f-848f980b1ab9","description":"A drove","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7620-8be5-fa0ecdbd9328","description":"A troop","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7f3c-8551-9896030122b3","description":"A run","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-778d-b50e-1736d210bea4","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Name the largest living bird.","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ostriches have only two toes on each foot, fewer than any other bird.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7eae-96ce-7425ab201eba","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7b13-850d-22d3cce6d9f2","description":"Peacock","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7540-a9e8-608f8a052384","description":"Emu","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-76e0-b71a-f8538131cf14","description":"Emperor Penguin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae88-7d34-8b3f-9314cb725518","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group 