ne, then used the distance between the cities to estimate Earth\'s circumference.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7173-a966-b5815f8759b7","description":"Eratosthenes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7f03-b654-e8878c23234f","description":"Euclid","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7763-b4ae-e3b7566f0564","description":"Ptolemy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70c0-ba7e-e3455cadb7c8","description":"Hipparchus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-75b6-bb7f-185179aef35a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which American physicist built the first working laser in 1960, using a ruby crystal?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Theodore Maiman\'s ruby laser used a flash lamp to excite the crystal, producing brief pulses of red light.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7104-b7ad-9c336f8a0aaf","description":"Theodore Maiman","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7173-8e1c-90459530fb4b","description":"Charles Townes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-74c5-8834-18f90e09b8fb","description":"Gordon Gould","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-73b5-99f7-dc503efc5807","description":"Arthur Schawlow","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79e6-b220-e4a7db45373e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where can we find the tympanic membrane?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The tympanic membrane vibrates in response to sound and passes those vibrations to the three small bones in the middle ear.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7d73-8cab-ce37507cb015","description":"Ear","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7891-9468-68eb232f8dcc","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7ad1-ad68-05437409bada","description":"Mouth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76d3-8557-8a8141118166","description":"Eye","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7b4b-8c4a-d1e4e4df2a02","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dc