here","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7d26-9d3c-6e59a8014a34","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Semiology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Semiology studies how signs convey meaning in communication and culture; the term is often used interchangeably with semiotics.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79ac-8474-423d11bf68b1","description":"signs","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7fa3-89bf-fde4429535de","description":"is concerned with earth materials that can be utilized for economic and\/or industrial purposes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-749a-bd08-e71bd8d331cf","description":"the practice of escaping from restraints or other traps","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c63-a6c8-ac9c166388e8","description":"a branch of logic focusing on part-whole relationships","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7b38-8af7-e8f9fca4145c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is enology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Enology is also spelled oenology; the term comes from the Greek word oinos, meaning wine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a1e-8216-ea281cfcbb1a","description":"Wine and winemaking","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76d8-87fc-2882792d6073","description":"Whales, dolphins and porpoises","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7ee3-9527-1ea183ccd321","description":"Gross and disgusting things","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7af2-9239-51cf436cee6b","description":"Tibet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7f96-9415-5091b5cebf0e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In geometry, what is the opposite of an acute angle?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"An obtuse angle measures more than 90 degrees but less than 180 degrees; an acute angle is less than 90 degrees.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-77fd-b0af-00025be492b5","description":"Obtuse","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7821-837e-f1a7c3f30f8d","description":"Chronic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-74e0-ba44-b23acc9bd734","description":"Vector","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-73ca-96fb-ec004d76ff31","description":"Integral","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-753b-bb17-fb7fbe9a3690","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What would you call a baby hare?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A leveret is born furred and with its eyes open, unlike a newborn rabbit, which is typically blind and hairless.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70d3-8923-b213c632ff74","description":"A Leveret","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7833-8693-1f28d48a627c","description":"A Codling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c8a-80e2-ba2753323246","description":"A Fawn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-72ac-a08c-c91f586fc016","description":"A Maggot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7daf-8c0a-fc0a14a8f6b0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What would you call a male bee?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A drone is a male honeybee. Unlike worker bees, drones do not gather pollen or have stingers.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79c0-a8e3-87dcb5ca8a1f","description":"A Drone","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7373-8960-bdf4bb78ceab","description":"A Buck","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-78c7-ac84-f9f46fd03371","description":"A Jack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7fa8-ab26-f3cbed0cfddf","description":"A Boar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7835-aba6-2971f829996d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is codicology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Codicology studies handwritten books as physical objects, including their materials, construction, and production; paleography focuses more on their handwriting.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7213-a539-16de940d95d2","description":"The preparation of books and manuscripts","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c91-87bf-0a31467c9279","description":"Water","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7318-8a00-3463096220fb","description":"The nature and origins of knowledge","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-73da-b88d-7608a44a1eef","description":"Microorganisms","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-73ec-98ba-01eb26114351","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical calcium carbonate often used for?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Limestone and marble are rich in calcium carbonate and have long been used in construction.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76cc-bcd4-b60d8b13e00b","description":"It is used as a building material.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7dc3-bd05-4f692fc8600a","description":"It is used to preserve food.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70ff-bf0b-47fef65b6540","description":"It is used to manufacture dry wall.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a93-9b13-30be33ed2468","description":"It is used in laundry detergent.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7962-83bb-8904ca65d63f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which bone is NOT part of the human skull?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Carpal bones form the wrist; the occipital and temporal bones are parts of the cranium, while the maxilla forms the upper jaw.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-712a-a477-1c3a5f3659a8","description":"Carpal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76e3-bad9-c6eade7a836c","description":"Occipital","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76ba-b11e-cb662294a63c","description":"Temporal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7f6c-8011-bf2c12a253dd","description":"Maxilla","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-71c9-9e6e-2988b380859a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What element is lacking in a diet when goitre occurs?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Iodine is needed to make thyroid hormones; a deficiency can cause the thyroid gland to enlarge, forming a goitre.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7969-97a3-65cc6a553a14","description":"Iodine","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-780f-a2ce-a191f99163e1","description":"Potassium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7117-b05e-d1656b99c5fe","description":"Chlorine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7af3-a088-447ca75e5054","description":"Iron","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7059-9176-f5d8a8d68dbd","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What protein is resposible for carrying oxygen in our blood?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hemoglobin contains iron-bearing heme groups that bind oxygen reversibly, giving red blood cells their color.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7047-878a-ca9f74a6e380","description":"Hemoglobin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76d2-9356-392f9b4f390e","description":"Histone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7ed6-a204-98165faa9c79","description":"Histidin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7db2-9066-8de8d04edd1f","description":"GABA","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79fd-9e78-cabaf01f1c66","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of mallards?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A sord is a traditional collective noun for mallards. Mallards are also the wild ancestors of most domestic duck breeds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e7a-9e15-413f08c937f9","description":"A sord","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7282-ab0d-4ff7b2475a8c","description":"A parliament","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-71a7-9299-6fae853aeae9","description":"A paddling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e07-9d9a-5d96e110cdae","description":"A skulk","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7875-a3da-940e86deaa02","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Orthopterology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Orthopterology concerns insects in the order Orthoptera; the name comes from Greek roots meaning \u201cstraight wing,\u201d referring to their forewings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7b7a-bd79-3c54f321bb6e","description":"grasshoppers and crickets","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7328-baea-979e81b4bb01","description":"the study and treatment of diseases of the urogenital tract","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7810-a562-2fc8c9027680","description":"the biosphere and its relations to the lithosphere and atmosphere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7146-918e-06ee19ce7a51","description":"male health and disease","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-739e-9a47-f141c9171a68","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Actinology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The term comes from Greek aktis, meaning \u201cray,\u201d and is associated with photochemistry, the study of light-driven chemical reactions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-740b-9c19-a59eb36b4fdd","description":"The effect of light on chemicals","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79de-8ba7-f112b777448f","description":"Animal behaviour","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e19-869e-0d9797bec525","description":"Ticks and mites","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c99-b1ac-3f6c0c31cb03","description":"Fresh water environments","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7347-8f9f-b54a83b00109","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a male falcon known as?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Tiercel comes from a word meaning \u201cthird,\u201d traditionally explained by the male being about one-third smaller than the female.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7991-920d-4aebe70e7344","description":"A Tiercel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-77b9-8c9f-f6b4293dc1ae","description":"A Jack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7137-b566-e7474ad8a3b5","description":"A Cob","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7ebd-9850-ee075fc4d779","description":"A Boar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-71b1-b213-014e1b5b9469","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which German physician identified the bacterium that causes tuberculosis in 1882?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Koch\'s postulates set out criteria for showing that a specific microorganism causes a particular disease.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7ffb-b5f5-11a44886235f","description":"Robert Koch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7f8f-9bdb-b453c4d05603","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-78be-b450-48f27453df5c","description":"Joseph Lister","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a40-b8ba-6502e28a94b1","description":"Paul Ehrlich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-74fc-865b-68d6236fc53a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of nightingales?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A watch is the traditional collective noun for nightingales, one of many whimsical English names for groups of birds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c0d-8bb0-174450dc1014","description":"A watch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7d73-b72f-d1e2a0048125","description":"A charm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7fd9-9762-068857b03331","description":"A rag","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7869-9369-3bfb07491507","description":"An exaltation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c03-b5af-b549a9635109","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of cattle?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A drove is a group of livestock being moved together; a gaggle is geese, a pride is li