 to oxen, and a stud to breeding horses.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7cb4-8850-25b0b68cab65","description":"A skulk","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70cd-b9f9-dc465963518f","description":"A school","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-706f-bf4f-76c41701e858","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-72af-b13a-c61418c2212d","description":"A stud","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7863-88d9-3ff486a0863b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Coleopterology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Beetles belong to the insect order Coleoptera; their hardened front wings, called elytra, protect the hind wings.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e3a-b3e3-3cd60b76e8bf","description":"Beetles","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-75d8-8ffd-0884fba42134","description":"The Shroud of Turin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-707c-b39f-d8724fc002e5","description":"Angels","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-753b-a655-e41b03bf91db","description":"The upper atmosphere","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7301-aa1a-9472d1ff56fc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which chemical element has the symbol Pa?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Protactinium\'s name means \u201cbefore actinium,\u201d reflecting that some of its isotopes decay into actinium.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70c5-884f-638900e67c45","description":"Protactinium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70fa-9776-88dcee27c965","description":"Potassium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7bce-b273-7570d5058f2c","description":"Lead","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-72f3-ae19-36b7c267afc6","description":"Palladium","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7424-9fa0-d6bb9e78340f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of bird is Hawaii\'s state bird, the Nene?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The nene is a goose native to Hawaii, with less-webbed feet suited to walking on rugged volcanic ground.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-794c-85c1-82123459fbcf","description":"A goose","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7828-94d7-288bb4b0479d","description":"A flamingo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-765f-a4b9-b1f5c6425c0c","description":"A pelican","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-731d-9e52-6737744073ca","description":"An ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e3f-ab96-95f4a9366e02","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical trinitrotoluene often used for?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Trinitrotoluene is used as an explosive filling in military shells, bombs, and grenades.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c62-b28f-93e460a66a81","description":"It is used in used in military shells, bombs, and grenades.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7fbf-82c3-f85dbf1b5476","description":"It is used in nuclear reactors, as a neutron moderator.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a31-99f8-a074363927d9","description":"It is used in disinfectants and antiseptics.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c91-8e66-506c607fb20d","description":"It is known to relieve pain and inflammation.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70fe-8a5a-86be4a984240","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who was the first director of the Los Alamos Laboratory in New Mexico?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Oppenheimer was a theoretical physicist who led the lab during the Manhattan Project and later advised the U.S. government on nuclear policy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7d4f-ae43-5f4e5b7cd2e1","description":"J. Robert Oppenheimer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7399-b91e-f8c7a5a8494b","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7923-bb23-d92fd93d7323","description":"Richard Feynman","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-754e-be74-f14dd67dd6ad","description":"Niels Bohr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7b06-9158-e8e69f926b06","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which constellation features Betelgeuse, the first star whose size was measured, in 1920?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Orion is traditionally depicted as a hunter, with Betelgeuse marking one shoulder. In 1920, Albert Michelson and Francis Pease measured Betelgeuse\u2019s apparent diameter using an interferometer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-791f-8899-ca7caf2626e5","description":"Orion","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e01-bd08-22b3d8eeeca4","description":"Draco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7dab-a2fe-87030bc14432","description":"Cassiopeia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7661-8537-d957190f0354","description":"Ursa Major","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-713b-9741-1f92dd8a2ba6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which part of the brain is most affected by a lobotomy?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The frontal lobe contains the prefrontal cortex, which supports planning and judgment. Lobotomies disrupted its connections and could cause major changes in personality and behavior.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-748e-95d1-9fb3c387996c","description":"Frontal lobe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7432-9a32-a4885bf45570","description":"Temporal lobe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a85-8852-32c0037d5ca5","description":"Occipital lobe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-75c4-9508-af0239bfdd61","description":"Cerebellum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7dfb-a5b8-6237442a1170","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which soft, purplish organ filters blood and stores platelets?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The spleen also supports immune defenses and removes aging red blood cells from circulation.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c5a-a932-d4463d123953","description":"Spleen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-73cb-94ad-45b44660a104","description":"Pancreas","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7a99-a277-cb67d85d56ec","description":"Gallbladder","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7dcb-a9df-976bd51dcaed","description":"Appendix","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70dc-b8f0-81632fd3c4da","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The \"canebrake\", \"timber\" and \"pygmy\" are types of what\"?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A rattlesnake\'s rattle is made of interlocking segments of keratin that vibrate when the tail shakes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7e2f-8fa0-6b5e04bc3ec6","description":"Rattlesnake","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70e7-b166-353a2f8bbea7","description":"Coyote","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7485-9bba-5ebbb0aab1bc","description":"Goose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-757e-8575-bebb91f2b150","description":"Pig","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7004-a9f9-93cc52fa8c1a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the unit of force?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The newton is named for Isaac Newton; one newton gives a one-kilogram mass an acceleration of one meter per second squared. Pascal measures pressure, joule energy, and watt power.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-736d-9665-27a73a4da6c6","description":"Newton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7214-ba05-4cbcd1bb4e5d","description":"Pascal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7660-aaba-778d91c92d57","description":"Joule","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76de-962f-9e0fca2a808e","description":"Watt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-78d8-9237-4a6888a45464","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Ethology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Animal behaviour is often studied in natural settings; Konrad Lorenz\'s research on imprinting in geese became a classic example of ethology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-71d3-98bf-9a428190b190","description":"Animal behaviour","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-79c2-a11b-93fd84479039","description":"The Earth\'s atmosphere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-70e3-8eed-641678b01528","description":"Glaciers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-78e0-8645-f9239f1034a1","description":"Friction and lubrication","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7840-9a4f-a7ef844e3fe6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Atmology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Atmology studies aqueous vapors in the atmosphere; weather is broader, encompassing wind, temperature, and precipitation too.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7446-b6e5-eba3dba58e98","description":"Aqueous vapors","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7d9d-8db8-d27282dc0527","description":"Insects","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7c33-8fb2-52d58cb0a21f","description":"The nervous system","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-743d-99f8-932f2a002234","description":"Weather","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-78c5-9f1f-a1423e13e9dc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these can be found in the knee?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The knee has medial and lateral menisci, which distribute load and help stabilize the joint.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7b44-8024-e4a4d4e9e8b2","description":"Meniscus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-74d9-9bf2-2f6a1bfc78c7","description":"Trochanter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-76a5-8333-be6cf09723a9","description":"Amygdala","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7bde-8d20-3e7bfcdb65b5","description":"Adenoid","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae89-7658-a6c5-b099